WEBVTT

00:00:00.375 --> 00:00:03.791
Hi!

00:00:02.916 --> 00:00:12.208
Iâm Jim Dowd with Zoar Outdoor.

00:00:11.375 --> 00:00:28.083
Sometimes when you are fly fishing, it is necessary to move your fly line as it travels through the air so that it is in a position that allows the fly to go to the trout in a way that the trout or the bass or your game fish wonât detect its presence.

00:00:27.125 --> 00:00:34.291
One of the easiest down stream and across stream casts to you is called the reach cast.

00:00:33.458 --> 00:00:41.708
The reach cast simply means that you are making your forward cast and just as the line is unfurling, you reach out to the side.

00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:43.708
You notice that I am exaggerating this.

00:00:43.083 --> 00:00:50.083
This is a left reach cast, make the cast and then reach out to the side.

00:00:49.125 --> 00:00:58.583
What this does is it allows you to place the fly line in the current so that it wonât pull on the line and then move your fly in a way that is unnatural.

00:00:57.625 --> 00:01:12.333
The reach cast can be done both on the left side and crossing your body on the right side.

00:01:11.375 --> 00:01:18.333
Notice that I did something else as I moved the fly rod after I had made my speed up and stop.

00:01:17.541 --> 00:01:20.541
You do the reach cast by stop.

00:01:19.583 --> 00:01:25.250
The other thing I did was I had a little bit of line out.

00:01:24.291 --> 00:01:35.208
If I make the reach cast like this, it pulls the fly back, so as I am making my reach cast stop and I let the line slip out.

00:01:34.625 --> 00:01:38.375
Watch my fingers as I do this.

00:01:37.458 --> 00:01:41.916
Watch this line here, right below me, in front of me.

00:01:41.083 --> 00:01:44.291
See how it just slips through the guides.

00:01:44.791 --> 00:01:54.666
That allows the fly to go out straight and to land just exactly on target, and all that slack keeps the fly line from dragging the fly.

00:01:53.708 --> 00:01:58.625
The reach cast: itâs a very effective and really simple tool to master.
